SUMMARY:Jack Jr. LIVE at Punch Line Houston
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Performer\nJack Assadourian Jr. — known on stage simply as Jack Jr. — is a rising star in the stand-up comedy world\, bringing a sharp\, self-deprecating wit and high-energy storytelling to stages across the country. \nBorn and raised in Southern California\, Jack Jr. has built a loyal following through his relatable observations about family\, relationships\, and the absurdities of everyday life. His comedy is clean enough for a broad audience yet edgy enough to keep things exciting. \nHe has performed at top comedy clubs nationwide including Cobb’s Comedy Club in San Francisco and the Ice House in Pasadena\, and is quickly becoming one of the most talked-about names on the club circuit. \nEvent Details\n\nDate: Thursday\, July 30\, 2026\nTime: 7:30 PM (Doors open at 6:30 PM)\nVenue: Punch Line Houston\nAddress: 1204 Caroline Street\, Houston\, TX 77002\nAge Restriction: 18+ (2 Beverage Minimum per person)\nTicket Prices: $38 – $50 (fees included)\n\nAbout the Venue\nPunch Line Houston is one of the premier stand-up comedy clubs in the South\, located in the heart of downtown Houston at 1204 Caroline Street. Part of the Live Nation family\, this intimate venue delivers an up-close comedy experience unlike any other in the city. \nThe club features a general admission layout with preferred seating options\, giving every guest a great view of the stage. The atmosphere is lively and social\, with a full bar and 2-beverage minimum that keeps the energy flowing throughout the show. \nParking is convenient — valet service is available at most shows\, and the Green Street garage (located on Clay between Main and Fannin) offers surface and garage parking with skybridge access. The venue is cashless and accepts all major credit cards. \nWhat to Expect\nExpect a high-energy evening of stand-up comedy featuring Jack Jr.’s signature blend of storytelling\, crowd work\, and sharp observational humor. The Thursday night show is a great way to kick off the weekend with laughs. \nDoors open one hour before the show\, so arrive early to grab your seats and enjoy a drink before the performance begins. The show typically runs approximately 90 minutes including an opening act. \nNote: Heckling\, cell phone use\, video recording\, and photography are strictly prohibited inside the showroom. Leave large bags and backpacks at home. \nTicket Information\nTickets range from $38 to $50 (all-in pricing\, fees included before taxes). Tickets are available through Ticketmaster (official) or VividSeats (resale). \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
