SUMMARY:Chris Porter LIVE at Punch Line Comedy Club - San Francisco
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you. \nAbout the Performer\nChris Porter is a Kansas City-born stand-up comedian known for his raw\, high-energy delivery and razor-sharp storytelling. He first gained national attention as a third-place finalist on NBC’s Last Comic Standing Season 4 in 2006\, and has since built a devoted following through his Comedy Central specials and appearances on Live at Gotham. \nPorter’s comedy is rooted in real life — vivid\, slice-of-life rants that transform everyday frustrations into precision-crafted laughs. His acclaimed hour Ugly and Angry cemented his reputation as a fearless\, no-nonsense voice in stand-up\, and his follow-up special A Man From Kansas doubled down on that unfiltered perspective. His most recent special\, There’s No Money in Babies (2023)\, showcases a comedian who keeps evolving while staying unmistakably himself. \nFans can expect a high-octane night of comedy filled with sharp observations\, relatable frustrations\, and the kind of honest\, blue-collar humor that has made Porter one of the most respected working comics in the country. \nEvent Details\n\nDate: Thursday\, July 30\, 2026\nShow Time: 8:00 PM\nVenue: Punch Line Comedy Club – San Francisco\nAddress: 444 Battery Street\, San Francisco\, CA 94111\nAge Restriction: 18+ (2 Beverage Minimum)\nTicket Prices: From $29 (General Admission)\n\nAbout the Venue\nThe Punch Line Comedy Club in San Francisco is one of the most storied comedy venues on the West Coast. Located at 444 Battery Street in the heart of the Financial District\, the club has been a launching pad for some of the biggest names in comedy since the 1970s. With an intimate capacity of around 300 seats\, every seat in the house feels close to the stage. \nThe venue features a classic comedy club layout with tiered seating\, cocktail tables\, and a full bar. The atmosphere is warm and lively — the kind of room where the energy between performer and audience crackles from the first joke. Parking is available in nearby garages along Battery and Front Streets\, and the venue is easily accessible via BART (Embarcadero Station) and Muni. \nThe Punch Line is a 18+ venue with a two-drink minimum\, so come ready to settle in\, order a drink\, and enjoy a world-class comedy experience in one of San Francisco’s most beloved rooms. \nWhat to Expect\nChris Porter’s live show is an experience unlike any other. Known for his rock-and-roll energy on stage\, Porter commands the room from the moment he walks out. His sets are a masterclass in comedic timing — building stories with precision before landing punchlines that hit hard. \nThis is a solo headlining show\, so expect a full evening of Chris Porter’s signature brand of comedy: honest\, unfiltered\, and deeply funny. Whether you’re a longtime fan or discovering him for the first time\, this is the kind of show you’ll be talking about for weeks. Doors typically open 60–90 minutes before showtime\, giving you time to grab a drink and find your seat. \nTicket Information\nTickets start at $29 for General Admission (18+ / 2 Beverage Minimum). Preferred Premium seating is also available at higher price points. Tickets are available through Ticketmaster (official) and VividSeats (resale). \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/chris-porter-live-at-punch-line-comedy-club-san-francisco/
LOCATION:Punch Line Comedy Club – San Francisco\, 444 Battery Street\, San Francisco\, California\, 94111\, United States Of America
