SUMMARY:James Austin Johnson LIVE at Punch Line Philly
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout the Performer\nJames Austin Johnson is one of the most exciting comedic talents to emerge from Saturday Night Live in years. A featured player on SNL since 2021\, Johnson has earned widespread acclaim for his uncanny impressions of political figures — most notably his portrayals of Presidents Biden and Trump\, which Vanity Fair called the “best Trump impersonation of all.” \nEntertainment Weekly described him as “a cross between Dana Carvey and Darrell Hammond\,” and his work on SNL has made him a household name among comedy fans. Beyond impressions\, Johnson is a sharp\, versatile stand-up comedian with a natural stage presence and a gift for storytelling. \nJohnson has also appeared in film and television\, including the Coen Brothers’ Hail\, Caesar! (2016) and the AMC hit series Better Call Saul. His multi-city comedy tour\, The Age of JAJ\, has been selling out venues across the country — and now he’s bringing the laughs to Philadelphia. \nEvent Details\nDate: Friday\, July 31\, 2026 \nTime: 7:30 PM EDT \nVenue: Punch Line Philly — 33 E. Laurel Street\, Philadelphia\, PA 19123 \nAge Restriction: 21+ with 2-beverage minimum \nTicket Prices: Starting from $38 (plus fees) \nAbout the Venue\nPunch Line Philly is Philadelphia’s premier stand-up comedy club\, located in the heart of the Northern Liberties neighborhood at 33 E. Laurel Street. The intimate venue seats approximately 300 guests and offers an up-close\, personal comedy experience unlike any large arena show. \nThe club features a full bar and two-drink minimum\, table seating arranged in a classic comedy club layout\, and excellent sightlines from every seat in the house. The atmosphere is lively and welcoming\, making it the perfect spot for a date night\, birthday celebration\, or a fun night out with friends. \nPunch Line Philly is part of the nationally recognized Punch Line Comedy Club brand and regularly hosts some of the biggest names in stand-up comedy. Parking is available nearby\, and the venue is easily accessible via public transit. Doors typically open 30–45 minutes before showtime. \nWhat to Expect\nJames Austin Johnson’s live show is a masterclass in comedic performance. Audiences can expect a full evening of stand-up comedy that blends sharp political satire\, pop culture observations\, and his legendary celebrity impressions — all delivered with the energy and polish of a seasoned SNL performer. \nThe show typically features an opening act before JAJ takes the stage for his headlining set. Fans who have seen him live rave about his ability to go beyond the impressions and deliver genuinely funny\, original material that keeps the crowd laughing from start to finish. \nThis is a 21+ event with a two-beverage minimum per person. Arrive early to grab your drinks\, find your seats\, and enjoy the full experience. Shows at Punch Line Philly tend to sell out quickly\, especially for high-profile headliners like JAJ. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: $38 – $75 (plus fees) \nTickets are available through Ticketmaster (official) and VividSeats (resale). Secure your seats before they sell out! \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/james-austin-johnson-live-at-punch-line-philly/
LOCATION:Punch Line Philly\, 33 E. Laurel Street\, Philadelphia\, PA\, 19123\, United States
